.policy "ruff-b003-assignment-to-os-environ" revision 2
.description "Don't assign a new value to os.environ; it doesn't change the real process environment, so update or clear the existing mapping instead."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff B003 (flake8-bugbear): `os.environ = …`. Rebinding the attribute replaces the module's mapping but not
// the process environment, which only the mapping's own methods change. Ruff reads the spelling, not the
// import: the target is exactly the Name `os` dotted with `environ`, and the statement has one target.
//   os.environ = {}            ← B003 at `os.environ`
//   environ = {}               not reported: a new meaning for a local name
//   o.os.environ = {}          not reported: `o.os` is not the Name `os`
//   a = os.environ = {}        not reported: two targets
#include "python/ast.rr"

.violation B003(at: node) code "B003"
    "Update `os.environ` in place with `.clear()` and `.update()` instead of assigning a new mapping to it."
    suppress ruff "B003"
B003(t) :- assign_target(a, t), !assign_ann(a, _), count : { assign_target(a, _) } = 1,
    attr_of(t, o, "environ"), kind(o, "identifier"), text(o, "os").
